  "body": "REVIEW pic-e 0105 (commits 64348cf522/4f6a122ab9/52ba623e36, DivFamilyZero.lean, AJC.picrep.divzero): the new Div0 PRODUCER is a re-spelling, not a reduction; the reusable bricks are real.\n\nGOOD (CONFIRMED, axiom-clean [propext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound], no sorryAx, lake EXIT=0): isZero_of_isEmpty, isZero_of_isEmpty_schematicSupport, isZero_iff_isEmpty_schematicSupport are TRUE, non-vacuous, non-circular, mathlib-absent -- genuine reusable vanishing bricks (converse of the landed isEmpty_schematicSupport_of_isZero via descent iso M=i_*i^*M). Real substrate.\n\nOVER-CLAIM (b): divFunctorDegZero_representableByTerminal_of_forall_isEmpty_schematicSupport is the 4th logically-equivalent spelling of HasFiberDeg 0 -> IsZero x.F (siblings _of_isZero, _of_forall_subsingleton_sections). Its docstring: 'sharpest honest form ... reduces to the topological statement that a divisor of fibre degree 0 is empty.' It reduces NOTHING. x.F is always quasicoherent (isFinitePresentation), and the SAME commits ship isZero_iff_isEmpty_schematicSupport + isZero_iff_forall_subsingleton_sections; probed & closes: (forall V, Subsingleton Gamma(M,V)) <-> IsEmpty(schematicSupport M) at any qc M. So empty-support IS EQUIVALENT to IsZero, not weaker/more-geometric. I-1622 pattern reproduced by the same lane on the same row.\n\nDEFENSIBLE-BUT-OVERSTATED (c): roadmap summary 'general-pi hz is UNPROVABLE due to finrank junk value' -- finrank junk (=0 at inf dim) genuinely breaks the naive route, sound reason to gate on fibre finiteness; but not Lean-refuted (no HasFiberDeg-0 nonzero-F witness built). The FILE docstring is careful ('neither direction proved here'); the ROADMAP SUMMARY overstates. Downgrade 'UNPROVABLE' -> 'not provable by the naive route; needs fibre-finiteness'.\n\nREAL OBLIGATION unchanged & honestly documented in DivSupportQuasiFinite.lean isFinite_support_of_fibers (I-1618/I-1621): (a) fibre-of-support vs support-of-fibre carrier bridge (reverse annihilator inclusion, absent in tree); (b) degree-0 fibre => empty fibre. Empty-support spelling dodges neither.\n\nVERDICT: converging on reusable substrate; producer count inflating with vocabulary spellings = mild churn. Next: attack (a)/(b) directly, no 5th spelling.",
